From fd7e782ee8d4d116e413380cd74d16d96948afc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:13:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 65/66] Per-step decision dump for the paired-episode analysis
 (EVAL.decision_dump, EVAL.teacher_forcing)

One JSON line per high-level step (policy probabilities over the graph,
argmax, DAgger expert choice, executed action, node/ghost positions) plus
one per finished episode (metrics, trajectory) in
<RESULTS_DIR>/decisions_<split>_r<rank>_w<world>.jsonl, from both the
ETP-R1 and the PriorGT/LLM trainers.  With EVAL.teacher_forcing True the
expert's choice is executed (its STOP stops at the current node), so two
policies see identical observations and are compared per step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013viJtZsLciemzz8VtLkwa1
